{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993714-using-mind-5-to-stop-dominate-or-presence-things","id":993714,"title":"Using mind 5 to stop dominate or presence things","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-26T14:50:49-07:00","id":993714,"title":"Using mind 5 to stop dominate or presence things","content":"So, how would you do this as a running thing up to and including mind 5. I could see creating like multiple minds in my own (so no paradox all using my inputs like eyes and such) and then have it so that when a dominate or presence effect hits that one, it switches to another?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:25:08-07:00","id":993769,"title":"","content":"First you need to decide which crossover rules your using and if you want to increase the Sphere requirements due to those.<br /> <br /> If you're not, Mind 1 and a lot of successes is usually good enough to impair such powers by having control over your mind (it's enough to multi-thread task your brain as it is). There's a Revised Matter 1/Mind 1 that makes you outright immune to emotional control (though with down sides like not being able to spend WP on anything because you've turned off too much of your head). Sure you could do something fancy like your multiple minds idea, but it's largely not necessary just to avoid being mind controlled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:26:07-07:00","id":993797,"title":"","content":"Life 4 is enough to stabilize/control your emotions (Or destabilize others.) if you have the right paradigm. For direct mind, Mind 1 IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T17:29:08-07:00","id":993798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993714-using-mind-5-to-stop-dominate-or-presence-things?p=993797#post993797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 4 is enough to stabilize/control your emotions (Or destabilize others.) if you have the right paradigm. For direct mind, Mind 1 IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>So along that thinking a Life4/mind 1 effect could effectively barricade such effects?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T18:46:25-07:00","id":993822,"title":"","content":"Life 4 isn't necessary, it's just an alternate option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T06:32:51-07:00","id":994009,"title":"","content":"I'd say Life 4 would be a brute force way to remove your ability to be affected by Presence. You turn off your bodily emotional responses, which are what that discipline acts on.<br /> <br /> Dominate directly attacks the mind without resort to emotional control, so Mind would be the only defense against it (save some fancy Prime/Entropy-ish effect to ward against generically vampiric powers). Mind 1 would be a basic defense, but you can do better with higher-level effects.<ul><li>Mind 2 would let you build a false front, allowing a vampire to think he's successfully gained control when he hasn't.</li> <li>With Mind 3, the illusion grows deeper, so a Dominate use that rifles through memories could be fooled into reading fictional ones. You could potentially use that time to create your own one-way telepathic link and read the vampire's surface memories instead.</li> <li>Mind 4 would let you delve deeper, pulling out forgotten events or buried secrets, as well as providing your mental defenses to others.</li> <li>With Mind 5, truly silly defenses are possible. You could forge a completely alternate mind, tailored to your needs Manchurian-candidate style, and place it in your body while you leave it to travel astrally. The vampire actually does gain control over that mind, but it only has the memories or impressions you gave it. In all ways he can detect, he's truly gained control and proceeds with his plan - until your embedded mental trigger activates at the worst time...</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T07:05:35-07:00","id":994017,"title":"","content":"The common, official as-written crossover rules demand a sphere rating equal to the rating of the discipline used against you.<br /> The common as-written crossover rules are also, IMO, horrible, as they completely ignore the fact that the sphere ratings are on a whole different scale of power and ability than Disciplines. They simply were a dumb-down solution of '4 = 4'.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I agree with what's mostly written so far. I also want to subscribe to Haldir's newsletter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T09:47:46-07:00","id":994081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993714-using-mind-5-to-stop-dominate-or-presence-things?p=994009#post994009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Life 4 would be a brute force way to remove your ability to be affected by Presence. You turn off your bodily emotional responses, which are what that discipline acts on.<br /> <br /> Dominate directly attacks the mind without resort to emotional control, so Mind would be the only defense against it (save some fancy Prime/Entropy-ish effect to ward against generically vampiric powers). Mind 1 would be a basic defense, but you can do better with higher-level effects.<ul><li>Mind 2 would let you build a false front, allowing a vampire to think he's successfully gained control when he hasn't.</li> <li>With Mind 3, the illusion grows deeper, so a Dominate use that rifles through memories could be fooled into reading fictional ones. You could potentially use that time to create your own one-way telepathic link and read the vampire's surface memories instead.</li> <li>Mind 4 would let you delve deeper, pulling out forgotten events or buried secrets, as well as providing your mental defenses to others.</li> <li>With Mind 5, truly silly defenses are possible. You could forge a completely alternate mind, tailored to your needs Manchurian-candidate style, and place it in your body while you leave it to travel astrally. The vampire actually does gain control over that mind, but it only has the memories or impressions you gave it. In all ways he can detect, he's truly gained control and proceeds with his plan - until your embedded mental trigger activates at the worst time...</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I regret that I have but one Like to give to this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T00:38:02-07:00","id":995541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/993714-using-mind-5-to-stop-dominate-or-presence-things?p=994081#post994081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div 